  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound 4-[(1S,4R,6R)-2,2,6-trimethyl-4-[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[[(2R,3R,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]oxan-2-yl]oxycyclohexyl]butan-2-one and the CD276 antigen, through a series of target interactions. This compound is identified as a target of multiple agents, including Eryvarin D, Kanshone H, and (1R,4R)-4-Hydroxydauca-7-Ene-6,9-Dione, all of which are implicated in targeting the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex is known to interact with CD276, a surface protein expressed on immune cells, and its inhibition has been shown to modulate immune responses. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially influencing CD276 expression or function. The strength of the evidence is supported by multiple independent pathways, but the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between the compound and CD276.",
